<title>USA: U.S. DAP VALUES SLIGHTLY HIGHER, AMMONIA UNCHANGED.</title>
<headline>U.S. DAP VALUES SLIGHTLY HIGHER, AMMONIA UNCHANGED.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diammonium phosphate values were slightly higher Monday and ammonia was unchanged.</p>
<p>DAP prices at the U.S. Gulf rose modestly in response to demand from fertilizer dealers in the U.S. Midwest.</p>
<p>&quot;Mississippi values are stronger because they are beginning fill-up for the fall,&quot; said one industry observer.</p>
<p>				 Dlrs/short ton   Chg from Friday</p>
<p>DAP central Fla		172-174		 up 2/unc</p>
<p>DAP central La Gulf	  186-188		 up 2/unc</p>
<p>Ammonia/La Gulf		175		     unc</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
